article.common-document
  header.header
    h2.title ToMMo JSV1 dataset
  .contents
    section.section
      h3.sectiontitle Summary
      p.body
        a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://jmorp.megabank.tohoku.ac.jp/docs/guide-en/dataset_detail/tommo-jsv1/') JSV1
        | is an allele and genotype frequency dataset of structural variants identified by long-read whole-genome
        | sequencing by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (ToMMo). TogoVar provides the frequencies on GRCh38.
      ul.unordered-list
        li Version: v20211208
        li Individuals used for frequency estimation: 222 unrelated individuals
        li Samples used for structural variant discovery: 333 samples from 111 trios
        li Analysis platform: Oxford Nanopore Technologies PromethION
        li Reference genome: GRCh38
        li Number of alternate alleles searchable in TogoVar (without the quality filter): 72,342

    section.section
      h3.sectiontitle Data analysis method
      p.body
        | DNA extracted from activated T lymphocytes was analyzed by long-read sequencing. Reads were aligned with LRA,
        | and structural variants of at least 50 bases were called with cuteSV. The structural variant repository was
        | built from 333 samples, while frequencies were estimated from the 222 unrelated parents to avoid double-counting
        | variants shared by parents and offspring.

    section.section
      h3.sectiontitle Data provider and terms of use
      p.body
        | See the
        |
        a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://jmorp.megabank.tohoku.ac.jp/downloads/tommo-jsv1-20211208-af') JSV1 allele frequency panel on jMorp
        | for dataset details, downloads, and terms of use. Some downloads may require acceptance of a Data Transfer Agreement.
